From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Flax <hmccanne@exclamationpoint.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ncsi: correct Mellanox single-port GMA MAC to base+2

The Mellanox OEM Get-MAC (GMA) response returns base_mac + (number of host
ports). On a dual-port ConnectX-4 OCP card that coincidentally lands on the
dedicated BMC management MAC (base+2), but on a single-port card it returns
base+1 (the unused second-port slot), leaving the BMC one short of the MAC
printed on the NIC label / expected by the host BIOS and OEM firmware.

The kernel applies no correction for Mellanox (unlike the BCM/Intel paths,
which already eth_addr_inc()). Bump the single-port Mellanox result by one so
it reaches base+2. The package channel count is fully enumerated by the time
the config-time GMA response is handled (TiogaPass has no mellanox,multi-host
DT property, so the probe-time GMA path is not used). This correction flows
into both dev_set_mac_address() and the perm_addr write added by
0015-ncsi-set-perm-addr-from-oem-gma, so dev_addr and perm_addr both land on
base+2. Dual-port and non-Mellanox cards are unaffected.

Signed-off-by: Flax <hmccanne@exclamationpoint.com>
---
--- a/net/ncsi/ncsi-rsp.c
+++ b/net/ncsi/ncsi-rsp.c
@@ -649,6 +649,21 @@
 	memcpy(saddr.sa_data, &rsp->data[mac_addr_off], ETH_ALEN);
 	if (mfr_id == NCSI_OEM_MFR_BCM_ID || mfr_id == NCSI_OEM_MFR_INTEL_ID)
 		eth_addr_inc((u8 *)saddr.sa_data);
+
+	/*
+	 * Mellanox OEM Get-MAC returns base_mac + (number of host ports): on a
+	 * dual-port card that lands on the dedicated BMC management MAC
+	 * (base+2), but on a single-port card it is one short (base+1, which is
+	 * the unused second-port slot). These ConnectX-4 OCP "Host Management"
+	 * cards always reserve base+2 as the BMC MAC (per the NIC label / what
+	 * the host BIOS and OEM firmware expect), so bump the single-port
+	 * Mellanox result by one to reach base+2. channel_num is fully
+	 * enumerated by the time the config-time GMA response is handled.
+	 */
+	if (mfr_id == NCSI_OEM_MFR_MLX_ID && ndp->active_package &&
+	    ndp->active_package->channel_num == 1)
+		eth_addr_inc((u8 *)saddr.sa_data);
+
 	if (!is_valid_ether_addr((const u8 *)saddr.sa_data))
 		return -ENXIO;
 
